<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Compass lifts pre-excepts yr shr, div falls.</title>
<headline>Compass lifts pre-excepts yr shr, div falls.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31 1997</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, attrib (cts)</p>
<p>excluding exceptional</p>
<p>    items			    23.6    vs   10.2</p>
<p>    Div (cts)			 4.5    vs    9.5</p>
<p>    (Loss)/profit for the yr  (56.64)  vs    0.89</p>
<p>    Tax				 0.05   vs    0.15</p>
<p>    Turnover			 60.64   vs   61.44</p>
<p>Full name: Compass Property Holdings Ltd (property)</p>
<p>NOTE - The directors declared a debenture interest payment of 28.1 cents per debenture unit in respect of the period October 1 1996 to March 31 1997.</p>
<p>The debenture interest will be payable on or about June 20 1997 to debenture holders registered in the books of the company on May 30.</p>
<p>Directors forecast profit before exceptional items for the coming year to reflect a slight improvement on that realised for the year ended March 31 1997.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
